  "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B014",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "for the conception and experimental realization of optical lattice clocks"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B011",
    "B045"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B014 combines a discrete physical solution—the magic-wavelength lattice clock, which permits many trapped atoms without sacrificing clock accuracy—with decisive experimental realization. It has passed the demanding tests that distinguish a proposal from an instrument: systematic effects are controlled, the platform has been independently realized, and it enables precision measurements of time, gravity, and fundamental physics. Katori's conceptual contribution and Ye's defining experimental advances remain a compact attribution for this bounded achievement.",
    "case_against": "The wider optical-clock revolution is an international enterprise with important contributors beyond these two names. The award must therefore recognize the lattice-clock concept and its decisive realization, not optical-frequency metrology as a whole. Historical examination of priority and contribution boundaries remains necessary before a final award.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig favors B032 because fluctuation relations provide a general, durable framework for irreversibility, while acknowledging that its experimental prominence must be weighed against mature precision platforms.",
        "response": "I agree that B032 is a substantial conceptual achievement and that generality has real scientific value. I nevertheless retain B014 because its central principle has generated a reproducible measurement capability whose systematic limits, physical reach, and performance can be directly examined across laboratories. The more tightly bounded discovery-to-demonstration chain makes its maturity and attribution stronger for this award."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson identifies circuit QED as a mature controllable light-matter platform, but notes unresolved credit involving Steven M. Girvin and overlap with other superconducting-circuit advances.",
        "response": "I share Johansson's assessment of circuit QED's experimental importance. His delimitation concern is decisive here: theory, architecture, and neighboring superconducting-circuit developments make a compact attribution difficult. B014 is more sharply defined by one physical solution and a two-person concept-to-realization account, without diminishing circuit QED as a serious future candidate."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth stresses that B014 suppresses trapping-induced clock shifts while retaining many atoms, and cautions that a future redefinition of the second should not be treated as an accomplished consequence.",
        "response": "I agree. The case does not require a future standards decision: independent realization, systematic control, and demonstrated precision applications already establish maturity. Her formulation also correctly keeps the citation centered on the specific lattice-clock solution rather than on the broader clock infrastructure."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether historical review confirms that Katori and Ye alone adequately delimit the magic-wavelength lattice-clock achievement amid other foundational optical-clock contributions.",
      "Whether the citation should explicitly name the magic-wavelength principle or retain the broader wording used here while preserving the same narrow boundary."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No conflict requiring recusal is apparent. My WACQT leadership overlaps institutionally with Göran Johansson's Chalmers environment, but the supplied record identifies no specific collaboration relevant to B014 or the alternatives."
  }
}
